<title>MOLDOVA: MOLDOVA T-BILLS SHOW MIXED TRENDS AT AUCTION.</title>
<headline>MOLDOVA T-BILLS SHOW MIXED TRENDS AT AUCTION.</headline>
<dateline>CHISINAU 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised yield on</p>
<p>Moldovan 28-day Treasury bills rose to 17.17 percent on Tuesday</p>
<p>from 14.50 percent on July 1, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>The yield on 91-day T-bills remained steady at 18.46</p>
<p>percent.</p>
<p>The yield on 182-day T-bills fell to 18.87 percent from</p>
<p>19.11 percent on July 1.</p>
<p>The yield on 364-day T-bills rose to 19.10 percent from</p>
<p>18.53 percent on June 17.</p>
<p>Full details of the 28-day T-bill auction--</p>
<p>				    July 8	     July 1</p>
<p> Issue volume		   2.00 mln lei     2.00 mln lei</p>
<p> Denominations		  1,000 lei	  1,000 lei</p>
